| File | Change | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `inventory.py` | Added `reserve()` — atomic check+decrement under `asyncio.Lock`; added `release()` to undo a reservation | Eliminates the TOCTOU race. `reserve()` holds a lock across the check-and-decrement, so stock can never go negative. `release()` restores stock on payment failure so other orders can claim it. |
| `payments.py` | Added `_charged_ids: set` to `__init__`; `charge()` now returns `True` immediately for a repeat `order_id` without double-recording | Idempotency guarantee — no order can be charged twice, even under retries. |
| `checkout.py` | Replaced check-then-charge-then-decrement with `reserve()` → `charge()` → `release()` on failure | Reserve-first ensures every successful charge has a corresponding item. If payment fails, the reservation is released so others can buy. |
